{"id": "85964", "name": "גזירה סתומה – dy/dx כאשר x=y−y³ (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Find \\(\\frac{d{{CT:0}}}{dx}\\) in terms of {{CT:1}} when \\(x\\) and {{CT:1}} are related by the following equation:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x = {{CT:2}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to \\(x\\), treating \\(y\\) as a function of \\(x\\) (chain rule), and then solve for the derivative.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Differentiating with respect to \\(x\\)</b><br>Differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to \\(x\\). The left-hand side gives \\(\\frac{dx}{dx}=1\\). On the right-hand side \\(y\\) is a function of \\(x\\), so by the chain rule each term is differentiated with respect to \\(y\\) and multiplied by \\(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ 1=\\left({{CT:3}}\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Solving for \\(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\)</b><br>Dividing by the bracket:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}={{CT:4}} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "q:v+v^3;", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "1/diff(p,v)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "-1/diff(p,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is the negative of what it should be. Have you mislaid a sign?</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You have found \\(\\frac{dx}{d{{CT:0}}}\\) not \\(\\frac{d{{CT:0}}}{dx}\\). To get \\(\\frac{dx}{d{{CT:0}}}\\) use the chain rule to get \\(\\frac{1}{\\frac{d{{CT:0}}}{dx}}\\).</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "Result-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "1/diff(q,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You appear to have used {@q@} instead of {{CT:5}}. The method looks fine but take care of the signs.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["p", "v"], "nvariants": 1}